,"login":"yashk2810","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE0MjYyNDE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yashk2810/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yashk2810/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yashk2810/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yashk2810/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yashk2810/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/yashk2810","user_view_type":"public"},"assignees":[{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/14262417?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yashk2810/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yashk2810/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yashk2810/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yashk2810/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/yashk2810","id":14262417,"login":"yashk2810","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE0MjYyNDE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yashk2810/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yashk2810/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yashk2810/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yashk2810/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yashk2810/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/yashk2810","user_view_type":"public"}],"author_association":"COLLABORATOR","body":"### Description\n\nIssue is pretty much what the title says - some combinations of instructions causes reshards to be inserted into a kernel. In my case, this causes lowering errors in Mosaic GPU (`reshard` is an unimplemented primitive).\n\nReproducer:\n```\nimport jax\nfrom jax import numpy as jnp\nfrom jax.sharding import PartitionSpec as PS, AxisType\nimport jax.experimental.pallas as pl\nimport jax.experimental.pallas.mosaic_gpu as plgpu\n\nmesh = jax.make_mesh((1, 1), (\"x\", \"y\"),\n                        axis_types=(AxisType.Explicit, AxisType.Explicit))\nwith jax.set_mesh(mesh):\n    x = jax.ShapeDtypeStruct(shape=(64, 64), dtype=jnp.float32,\n                                sharding=PS(\"x\", \"y\"))\n    @jax.jit\n    def trace_me(x):\n        x_spec = jax.typeof(x).sharding.spec\n        @jax.shard_map(in_specs=x_spec, out_specs=x_spec)\n        def shmap(x_shard):\n            def kernel(x_ref, o_ref, x_smem, barrier):\n                plgpu.copy_gmem_to_smem(x_ref, x_smem, barrier)\n                plgpu.barrier_wait(barrier)\n                x_value = x_smem[...]\n                x_smem[...] = jnp.where(x_value > 0, x_value, 0)  # Reshards added here\n                plgpu.commit_smem()\n                plgpu.copy_smem_to_gmem(x_smem, o_ref)\n                plgpu.wait_smem_to_gmem(0)\n            out_shape = jax.ShapeDtypeStruct(shape=(64, 64), dtype=jnp.float32)\n            result = plgpu.kernel(kernel,\n                out_shape=out_shape,\n                grid=(1,),\n                grid_names=(\"g\"),\n                num_threads=1,\n                thread_name=\"wg\",\n                scratch_shapes=dict(\n                    x_smem=plgpu.SMEM((64, 64), jnp.float32),\n                    barrier=plgpu.Barrier()\n                )\n            )(x_shard)\n            return result\n        return shmap(x)\n    print(jax.make_jaxpr(trace_me)(x))\n```\n\nThe `jnp.where` introduces reshards inside of the kernel. This is the jaxpr equation that gets produced for the `jnp.where` call:\n\n```\nr:f32[64,64] = jit[\n     ctx_mesh=Mesh('x': 1, 'y': 1, axis_types=(Explicit, Explicit))\n    jaxpr={ lambda ; q:bool[64,64] p:f32[64,64]\n        s:i32[]. let\n        t:f32[] = convert_element_type[\n        new_dtype=float32\n        weak_type=False\n        ] s\n        u:f32[64,64] = reshard[\n        concrete_mesh=None\n        dst_sharding=NamedSharding(mesh=AbstractMesh('x': 1, 'y': 1, axis_types=(Manual, Manual), device_kind=NVIDIA H100 80GB HBM3, num_cores=132), spec=PartitionSpec(None, None))\n        ] p\n        v:f32[64,64] = broadcast_in_dim[\n        broadcast_dimensions=()\n        shape=(64, 64)\n        sharding=NamedSharding(mesh=AbstractMesh('x': 1, 'y': 1, axis_types=(Manual, Manual), device_kind=NVIDIA H100 80GB HBM3, num_cores=132), spec=PartitionSpec(None, None))\n        ] t\n        r:f32[64,64] = select_n q v u\n    in (r,) }\n] q p 0:i32[]\n```\n\n### System info (python version, jaxlib version, accelerator, etc.)\n\njax:    0.9.1.dev20260204+ee41a31ac (on my own fork)\njaxlib: 0.9.0\nnumpy:  2.4.2\npython: 3.12.3 (main, Nov  6 2025, 13:44:16) [GCC 13.3.0]\ndevice info: NVIDIA H100 80GB HBM3-8, 8 local devices\"\nprocess_count: 1\nplatform: uname_result(system='Linux', node='ip-10-100-58-215', release='6.14.0-1017-aws', version='#17~24.04.1-Ubuntu SMP Wed Nov  5 10:48:17 UTC 2025', machine='x86_64')","closed_at":"2026-02-04T16:06:48Z","closed_by":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/44061?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/copybara-service%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/copybara-service%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/copybara-service%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/copybara-service%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/copybara-service","id":56741989,"login":"copybara-service[bot]","node_id":"MDM6Qm90NTY3NDE5ODk=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/copybara-service%5Bbot%5D/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/copybara-service%5Bbot%5D/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/copybara-service%5Bbot%5D/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/copybara-service%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/copybara-service%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","type":"Bo